[Music]  hello there free to play video games can  be a bit of a minefield for every great  game we see we get at least seven which  aren't so great so i thought i'd show  you 10 games that look to be excellent  free-to-play experiences for you and  your friends some games are coming out  this summer others are due in 2023 if  you'd like me to cover any of these in  detail please let me know in the  comments now let's do this  coming this summer is disney speedstorm  imagine a cross-platform mario kart  starring characters from disney and  pixar sounds pretty good right each of  the tracks is based on iconic locations  from the animated movies and tv shows  and the roster is absolutely packed  mickey can race sully from monsters inc  captain jack sparrow can go up against  donald duck it's weird in the best kind  of way like mario kart the characters  have slightly different stats but that's  where speedstorm pivots as each racer  has their own specific skills and  abilities and we've seen a few ultimate  abilities too each new season will bring  new tracks and new characters which will  likely be where we start paying for  content to my surprise split screen  couch co-op is confirmed and cross play  is here too on playstation xbox switch  pc and mobile summer can't come soon  enough  [Music]  as we're already comparing these new  games to nintendo products let's  continue back in december i showed you  multiverses a two on two platform  fighter which takes on the smash bros  formula multiverses is due to release  any moment now on playstation xbox and  pc and lets us choose to fight with a  host of characters from warner brothers  owned franchises this means batman can  fight shaggy from scooby-doo on release  there will be at least 13 playable  characters with more coming regularly to  keep the meta changing and players on  their toes if multiverses is successful  we can expect to see mortal kombat  characters joining the fight or even  lord of the rings alumni each character  has their own abilities and the synergy  between each pair is important or if you  don't want to play with a teammate it  can be a free-for-all instead  multiverses is releasing this year it  could be releasing any minute now i'll  keep you updated  [Music]  have a look-see at spine a team-based  action game set in this dystopian  technology-filled world spine technology  turned standard human beings into super  beings with improved reflexes we are  told that martial arts movies have  inspired the melee focused combat and  the gun-fu seen in films like the matrix  is implemented throughout so dodging  bullets looks to be a real option here  before getting up close and personal  with a katana in hand the devs want the  game to feel like a movie as well as a  competitive pvp experience spine has  been confirmed for ps5 xbox series pc  and mobile we'll find out more in late  2022 cyberpunk gunfu and samurais spine  could be a massive hit  [Music]  a game i'm watching and hoping to be  great is exo mecca a first-person  shooter where futuristic soldiers do  battle on a newly found untouched planet  the gun play looks solid and the sheer  breadth of things we've seen is just wow  underwater caves for flanking maneuvers  so many vehicles to drive like tanks and  helicopters oh and like the name  suggests this freaking mechs here it'll  be like being in the scene from the  transformers movie originally this was  only planned for pc but it's now coming  to xbox and there are reports of ps5 too  but i don't trust those sources right  now the release date for exomecha has  already been pushed back a few times it  was due out last month it appears that  further funding is allowing the team to  create a bigger game than we first saw  so now we play the waiting game a  release date is due my guess is this  free-to-play game will be coming in 2023  [Music]  another free game to look out for in the  summer is gundam evolution i know  there's been some questionable gundam  games in the past but from the people  who've played the beta so far it's  actually fun gundam evolution is a six  on six hero shooter the feedback  suggests evolution is heavily inspired  by overwatch from the hud to the map  layout and the skills of each unit each  gundam has a different health pool dash  limit and preferred range of combat and  on release three game modes are  confirmed point capture domination and  destruction i'll tell you more about  those when the game releases in a month  or two like usual it's another  cross-platform release on ps4 ps5 all  the xboxes and pc as well  starting this summer another  free-to-play disney game is coming to  take over your life disney dreamlight  valley basically over time all the  disney characters have forgotten about  each other and the world they live in  that's where you rock up and bring  everyone back together it appears that  dreamlike valley is a cross between a  typical adventure game with quests and  something like the sims or animal  crossing we haven't seen any gameplay  mechanics just yet but if you want to  sign up to be a founder or if you have  xbox game pass you'll be the first to  play in july with the full release  scheduled for 2023. it's going to be on  every platform from playstation to  android from switch to ios i just hope  they don't make me collect turnips like  animal crossing that was too hardcore  [Music]  i started this video by showing you a  cart racing game set to be big well it  turns out that that space is quite  competitive thanks to cart rider drift  just like disney's speedstorm the vibe  is most definitely mario kart but unlike  speedstorm kart rider is much more  closer to the iconic cart races of the  past power-ups can be found on the road  and shortcuts play an important part to  stay competitive especially on harder  settings drift is going all out on  customization and making that the center  of their business plan as the other kart  racer is scheduled for summer it's  likely that cartwright adrift will  release before that to try and maximise  their time in the sun if you want to  play now you can sign up for it or you  can wait for the full release set for  the summer on ps4 ps5 xbox and pc  [Music]  my most anticipated free-to-play game of  2022 is arc raiders a co-operative  third-person shooter in which we are a  group of raiders who must fight back  against the onslaught of ark a ruthless  machine threat descending from space  we'll be scavenging the ruins of a  forgotten world to somehow find a way to  outsmart our new enemies celeste is the  face of the game someone who lost  everything to ark and then became a  resistance fighter the game is also  based on a book of the same name in  march the play testing for the full game  began which if all goes well should see  arc raiders pop up again soon with a  release date until then all we know is  that it's coming in 2022 on ps5 xbox  series and pc when epic games closed  down paragon in favour of fortnite there  was a bunch of that community left with  nothing to play that's where over prime  comes in a moba an online battle arena  that takes inspiration from dota league  of legends and paragon over prime is  actually already out on pc right now but  the real reason i'm including it in this  video is due to this footage the  overprime team are currently working on  a console port here it is on the ps5 dev  kit being used to play a full match  no console release date just yet 2022  maybe  and finally for game 10 it's another  title which was due to release earlier  this year but at the very last second in  february it was pulled and now once  again we are waiting a new release date  all we know for certain is it's coming  in 2022. this is rumble verse a battle  royale game but guns are replaced with  wrestling moves 40 players crash down  into the city as the usual storm circles  push everyone closer and closer together  until only one is left standing it  doesn't take itself too seriously at all  rumble verse is all about customization  and looking however you want there is a  crazy amount of flexibility from skin  color body shape and hairstyles right  down to elbow pads and the color of your  underwear  which we all know is very important i  played a few of the rumble verse tests  and it was certainly lacking something  which made you want to come back for  game after game after game but if they  do find the trigger to make people want  to play constantly i believe rumble  verse will be huge and it has the  backing of epic games if rumble verse  interests you be sure to check back next  month because i have a full breakdown  coming so there we have it 10  free-to-play games that i believe are  worth your time releasing between now  and summer next year thank you very much  for watching to the end i'm adam you're  awesome it's been a pleasure i'll see  you next time  [Music]

